<.shell current={:field_definitions}>
  <h1>Field definitions</h1>
  <p class="lead">What each custom field on a team's records is, never its values.</p>

  <h2>The list</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.field_list
      id="field-definitions-sample"
      fields={custom_field_definitions()}
      path={fn _field -> "#" end}
      team_name="Coast Range SAR"
      organization_name="WESARA"
    />
  </div>

  <h2>One field</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.field_details
      field={custom_field_definitions() |> List.last()}
      timezone="America/Vancouver"
      team_names={%{11 => "Coast Range SAR"}}
      organization_name="WESARA"
      team_name="Coast Range SAR"
      restricted_text="Only team admins see its values. Members and your organization never do."
    />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    The Fields pages in settings, for a team or an organization (#872). The list is an index to scan, one
    <a href={page_path(:row_link)}>row link</a>
    per field: its name, its type in grey, at most one tag, and the first line of what it means. On a member field the
    grey text also says what members do with their own answer. The tag is Needed to publish on an activity's field, or
    else Restricted on an activity's or an item's. On a team's page its own fields come first, under its name, then its
    organization's. The fields in no group come first in each, then each named group under its title, as on a record's
    Fields tab.
  </p>
  <p>
    A row opens the field's own page, a detail list in one order that leaves out what a field lacks: what it means, its
    type, what it's on, who added it, needed to publish, members, restricted, and every choice, one per line. Who added
    it, needed to publish, members, and restricted each carry a line on what they mean. A choice a team added to its
    organization's field is listed under the team's name.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A record's own values. Those are the record's Fields tab, a <a href={page_path(:detail_list)}>detail list</a>. Never a
    select to show a field's choices: nothing here can be changed.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.field_list&gt;</code>
    takes one kind's fields, with their groups preloaded, and a <code>path</code>
    function to each field's page. <code>team_name</code>
    and <code>organization_name</code>
    split it by who owns each field. <code>&lt;.field_details&gt;</code>
    is the field's own page.
  </p>
</.shell>
